                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Ughh. where to begin...\n\nI love the idea of this game.  But that's all I can love about it... \n\nGraphics are decent, no complaints about the audio. \n\nSo darn tedious, and not in a fun intricate detail kind of way... but more of a OMG how many more times do i have to do the SAME DARN THING....  I played the first two missions.  \n\nYou lay down road cones, I don't even know how many, but you have to pick one up from the truck, and place it on the marker, simple, yes.. but after 20 I think we get the point.  Place a few cones, drive the truck forward, place a few cones, drive the truck forward rinse and repeat.  Next part of the mission is painting lines, basically it's grabbing the paint machine lining it up and walking in a straight line pressing space at the beginning of each line, once you get a rythym going it's a peice of cake, and goes by relatively quickly.  \n\nMission 2-  you have to repair some rough spots on a bike path, you have to use a jackhamer, that's pretty cool, but you seem to walk slower and after about the 4th spot you've got to clear out, you start wondering WTF why did I buy this.  Then you finally get to the end, just to find out that now you have to go over all the areas you dug up with some sort of asphalt machine, ,then again with the machine and some tar or something.  I dunno, i was running on autopilot at that point.   Finally completed the mission after about a half hour of repetition.\n\nI'll try the next mission at another time, I need a break from this now, definitley has it's spot in the sim world, but at the same time it needs a lot more variety  For right now I'd say skip this one and grab a different sim.  Should the dev's make any major changes / improvements I'll re-evaluate my review and update accordingly.",
